        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 8,
        "titulo": "Ordering food: the accusative in action",
        "explicacao": "When you order or say what you eat, the food goes into the accusative (the direct object). Only feminine words in -а change: -а becomes -у. Masculine and neuter nouns that are not living beings stay the same: «Я хочу рис», «Я хочу мясо», «Я хочу салат». English never marks this, so it is easy to forget: the word after the verb must change when it is feminine.",
